      "raw_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine Raymond's current age.**\nWe are given that Samantha is currently 31 years old.\nWe are also told that Raymond was born 6 years before Samantha.\nTherefore, Raymond is 6 years older than Samantha.\n$$ \\text{Raymond's Age} = 31 + 6 = 37 \\text{ years old} $$\n\n**Step 2: Determine when Raymond's son was born.**\nRaymond had a son at the age of 23.\nTo find out how many years ago this happened, we subtract his age at the time of the son's birth from his current age.\n$$ \\text{Years ago} = \\text{Raymond's Current Age} - \\text{Raymond's Age at Son's Birth} $$\n$$ \\text{Years ago} = 37 - 23 = 14 $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nRaymond's son was born 14 years ago.\n\n#### 14<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "Here is the step-by-step solution to the problem:\n\n**Step 1: Determine Raymond's current age.**\nWe are given that Samantha is currently 31 years old.\nWe are also told that Raymond was born 6 years before Samantha.\nTherefore, Raymond is 6 years older than Samantha.\n$$ \\text{Raymond's Age} = 31 + 6 = 37 \\text{ years old} $$\n\n**Step 2: Determine when Raymond's son was born.**\nRaymond had a son at the age of 23.\nTo find out how many years ago this happened, we subtract his age at the time of the son's birth from his current age.\n$$ \\text{Years ago} = \\text{Raymond's Current Age} - \\text{Raymond's Age at Son's Birth} $$\n$$ \\text{Years ago} = 37 - 23 = 14 $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nRaymond's son was born 14 years ago.\n\n#### 14",
